  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNICEF Partnership - Girls in School are Supported (P4-5)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls in school(P4-5),the intervention will reach the most learning disadvantaged in-school girls and boys in P4-5.There is a strong evidence demonstrating that targeted support to girls in school can improve self-confidence. retention and learning outcomes, including some evidence from Rwanda. In Rwanda, there is evidence that targeted remedial learning works to improve learning outcomes. UNICEF, in partnership with the Imbuto foundation is implementing a remedial education programme to accelerate learning recovery. The programme targets marginalised girls in P3-P6 who perform below basic in literacy and numeracy assessment (bottom 20%).</narrative>
  </description>
